  "evidence": "Mentions UKIP by name and founding year (\"UKIP, founded in 1993\"), core pledge to repeal the European Communities Act 1972 and keep the pound, opposition to an EU government/army/constitution, and the signature \"Independence Dividend\" of about £20bn with detailed allocations (e.g., +£2bn NHS, 30,000 teachers, 25,000 police, −9p/litre fuel duty). It references early‑2000s issues such as opposing the partial sell‑off/PPP of the London Underground, scrapping compulsory metrication, rejecting EU Corpus Juris/Europol, repealing and re‑enacting the Human Rights Act to align with British common law, exiting the CAP/CFP with a 200‑mile limit, and leaving the EU Rapid Reaction Force while prioritising NATO/US interoperability.",
